  "implementation": [
    "ForeignEarly selects the native root single-write INSERT path from the original statement before source/candidate lowering. SELECT, multiple rows, RETURNING and programs retain the general statement-counter boundary.",
    "A pure accepted-candidate check uses the ordinary constraint/conflict executor and discards temporary state. Child parent lookup precedes any parent scan, permitting a matching NEW self key and NULL while preventing an old orphan from canceling a missing new parent.",
    "Replacement eligibility uses actual source rowid targets, declared key metadata and unique indexes. Native insert.c supplies ipkColumn for an explicit NULL; an omitted key can avoid compiled replacement writes. The original input metadata is retained before all-column candidate normalization.",
    "The real point and its connection effects execute only after the early lookup succeeds. The existing state-carrying API retains late point rowids for statement-counter paths. No native production function or shim change is introduced."
  ],
  "evaluation_protocols": {
    "public_file_modes": "7100 stdout/exit/first-error and independent persisted catalog/row/integrity comparisons in rollback/WAL modes, including 48 early FK cases; both public drivers stop at error.",
    "same_connection": "62 memory-connection comparisons use the actual Core state-carrying API and pinned non-bailing shell; subsequent SQL observes data and connection counters. Fresh final generated inputs are recorded separately from fixed controls.",
    "separate_diagnostics": "136 additional fixed matrix probes are retained independently and are not included in the 62 or 7100 totals.",
    "named_features": "The retained 88 named probes still have eight failures and are not a global coverage percentage."
  },
  "proof_scope": "All retained contracts and audits compile. An added audited component law disables the early path when FK checking is off. An additive maintained executable group checks early data/counter/rowid preservation, matching NEW self keys and omitted versus explicit-NULL replacement keys. No global FK equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "Wider error codes/phases, FAIL/IGNORE/ROLLBACK controls, triggered UPSERT, INSTEAD OF/temp triggers, writable CTEs, trigger-aware ALTER and deferred private-function declarations remain work.",
    "Eight of 88 named probes still fail: WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys and partial/expression indexes, both modes. These probes do not define global coverage.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical allocations and earlier SQL/storage limitations remain. The finite process-kill samples do not establish every syscall/power-loss schedule."
  ],
